Port of _patches/typescript/013-tsoptions-parsinghelpers.patch (tsc/internal/tsoptions/parsinghelpers.go) to tsrs.

- MergeCompilerOptionsCallback / RegisterMergeCompilerOptionsCallback: tsrs_tsoptions::MergeCompilerOptionsCallback
  (an Arc'd closure behind a process-wide RwLock, as patch 002's callback) and
  register_merge_compiler_options_callback. merge_compiler_options takes the source config path and base path and
  calls it after the field merge, as Go's mergeCompilerOptions does.
- ParseCompilerOptions: a `plugins` key (strings.EqualFold) sets CompilerOptions::effect from
  ets_etscore::parse_from_plugins (patch 007).
- tsrs-only: the `impl ets_etscore::AnyValue for CompilerOptionsValue` that parse_from_plugins needs for Go's `any`
  type assertions (the orphan rule puts it here: ets_etscore cannot depend on tsrs).
- tsrs has no mergeParsedCompilerOptions (its callers call merge_compiler_options directly; see patch 025), and its
  parsinghelpers tests do not call merge_compiler_options, so the test hunks have no counterpart.

